class.description:
[VideoWindowSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"video_window"[/code]: it stores the window and display options chosen by the player, loads them when the game starts and applies them to [DisplayServer] and the root window. The settings resource is a [VideoWindowSettings]. The file is [code]user://settings/video_window.ini[/code] by default.
The domain is applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_PRE_DISPLAY], before the display server exists: the main window is created with the stored mode, size, V-Sync mode and window flags, and it is placed on the stored screen before it is shown, so it opens without a visible jump. The content scale and the HDR values are applied as soon as the root window exists ([constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE]).
Changes of [member VideoWindowSettings.window_mode], [member VideoWindowSettings.window_size] and [member VideoWindowSettings.screen] go through the confirmation of [SettingsServer]: in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_MODE_IMMEDIATE] they are applied at once, and they are reverted after [code]settings/general/confirmation_timeout[/code] seconds unless the game calls [method SettingsServer.confirm_changes] (for example from a "Keep these settings?" dialog). Connect to [signal SettingsServer.confirmation_requested] to show the dialog.
The command line wins over the stored values: [code]--fullscreen[/code], [code]--maximized[/code], [code]--windowed[/code], [code]--resolution[/code], [code]--screen[/code], [code]--position[/code], [code]--always-on-top[/code] and [code]--disable-vsync[/code] are set as session overrides (see [method SettingsServer.set_session_override]): applied but never saved. A game embedded in the editor keeps the placement of the editor.
Further windows (an inventory window, a second screen) are stored by node path in [member VideoWindowSettings.window_states]: call [method save_window_state] when the player moved or resized one, and the window gets its mode, size, position and screen back when it enters the scene tree again. [method restore_window_state] restores a window on demand, also before it is added to the tree (pass a key then).
Without free windows (Android, iOS, Web, headless) the size, position, screen and window flags are stored but not applied; see [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported]. On the headless display server all values are kept by the domain and returned by [method SettingsServer.read_from_engine].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _on_fullscreen_toggled(toggled_on):
	if toggled_on:
		VideoWindowSettingsServer.set_window_mode(DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN)
	else:
		VideoWindowSettingsServer.set_window_mode(DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_WINDOWED)

func _on_resolution_selected(size: Vector2i):
	VideoWindowSettingsServer.set_window_size(size)

func _on_keep_pressed():
	VideoWindowSettingsServer.confirm_changes() # Saved now.
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
private void OnFullscreenToggled(bool toggledOn)
{
    VideoWindowSettingsServer.SetWindowMode(toggledOn ? DisplayServer.WindowMode.Fullscreen : DisplayServer.WindowMode.Windowed);
}

private void OnResolutionSelected(Vector2I size)
{
    VideoWindowSettingsServer.SetWindowSize(size);
}

private void OnKeepPressed()
{
    VideoWindowSettingsServer.Singleton.ConfirmChanges(); // Saved now.
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
